// Shared lifting guidance admitted by the native coding controller.
section [form.bml] {
 class FormLift {
  def fl-guidance() = "FORM/BML LIFTING: Preserve observable behavior, public names, evaluation order, ownership and release. Read callers and the supplied helper contracts first. Author section [form.bml] with def, lexical lambdas, lazy ?: and ??, exact-value match arms, [item,...] lists, rows[index] access, half-open start .. end ranges, infix arithmetic/comparisons, and input-last |> when they make intent clearer. Lists and indexing lower directly to existing native primitives; named accessors own the meaning of tuple positions. Use (String), (Number) or (Value) comparison contracts where the type matters. Parenthesize each boolean pair; and/or primitives take two operands. Reuse core map(f,rows), filter(pred,rows), foldl(f,initial,rows), any?(pred,rows), all?(pred,rows) and range(start,end) instead of another recursive walk. Closures carry context; an existing carried-argument API can remain a thin adapter. Use classes to group a coherent API and higher-order functions for shared behavior. Use BMF cursors and the shared expression grammar for source scans; retain original spans and verify compiler recipe identity. Templates describe parameters and members; they do not manufacture instance accessors, interface checking or specialization. Name domain literals once at their semantic owner; keep ordinary arithmetic identities direct. Missing is nothing(), distinct from zero, false and an empty row. Keep repair in the same choice/checkpoint with its original evidence. Remove superseded implementations after callers and behavioral checks agree. Compact expression serves readability and measured work, not character count. Native tools operate on supplied resident documents; model-selected commands, providers and network access are absent. Read the returned candidate and actual checks before claiming a lift. ";
 }
}
